{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And I.</b> Like the sense of \"against YHWH and against His anointed\" (Psalms 2:2)." "<b>Comes.</b> The word עת is missing, and the meaning is: when they reckon that they are established against me, then a time will come to gather all the nations around Jerusalem." "<b>And they shall see My glory.</b> That I shall execute judgment upon them until they see my glory throughout all the world, and this is the war of Gog and Magog."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 66, :notes {1 "The note צ\"ל עת indicates that the word printed as עם in the base text should be read as עת (\"time\"); Ibn Ezra's comment itself glosses the missing word as עת."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:18.074935786Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}